+## Clarifications
+
+### Session 2026-11-20
+
+- Q: How should the tool decide that an output file would overwrite one of the input files it was asked to redact (FR-049)? → A: By filesystem identity — resolve both paths and compare the actual file on disk, so differently-spelled paths, symlinks, and hard links are all caught.
+- Q: Should the tool check that the output folder is usable and that no output file would overwrite an input file before writing any output file, or check each input as it reaches it (FR-048, FR-049, FR-050)? → A: Check the folder and every operand's output path up front before any output file is written; genuine read/write failures discovered later still leave earlier completed files on disk.
+- Q: Do only the digits `0`-`9` count toward a phone number's 8-to-15 digits, or do digits from other writing systems count too (FR-033, FR-034)? → A: Only `0`-`9`, matching the existing email, IPv4, and card rules; a digit from another writing system neither forms part of a candidate nor triggers the followed-by-a-digit exclusion.
+- Q: Does the existing speed expectation of 100,000 lines in under 30 seconds also apply to `--out-dir` runs (SC-007, SC-018)? → A: Yes — the same budget applies, measured across all FILE operands of a single run together.
+
