+**Order of checks**
+
+- **FR-054**: With `--out-dir`, the tool MUST perform the checks it can make in advance before
+  it opens or writes any output file, in this order:
+  1. a help request (FR-051) and command-line usage errors (FR-040, FR-047) are handled first,
+     and leave the filesystem untouched;
+  2. `DIR` is then created if absent and confirmed usable as a directory (FR-042, FR-048),
+     before any input source is read;
+  3. the output path computed for every FILE operand is then checked against that operand under
+     FR-049a, and a collision in any operand fails the run before any output file is opened and
+     before any input source is read.
+
+  Consequently a run that fails at step 2 or step 3 MUST NOT have written, replaced, or
+  truncated any output file, and a collision in a later operand MUST NOT leave output files
+  written for earlier operands. A run that reaches step 3 cleanly MUST then stream each FILE
+  (FR-041, FR-044); failures discovered only during that streaming — an unreadable FILE
+  (FR-050) or an output file that cannot be written (FR-048) — retain the existing behaviour of
+  leaving output files already completed for earlier operands on disk. The tool MUST NOT delete
+  or roll back output files it has already written.
